CP/M 2.2 — Provenance and License
====================================

Source of CCP+BDOS binary (cpm22-64k.bin)
-----------------------------------------

Assembled from the Z80 disassembly of CP/M 2.2 by Clark A. Calkins
(reconstructed from memory image, February 27, 1981), obtained from the
Unofficial CP/M Website at https://www.cpm.z80.de/ (file cpm2-asm.zip).

The only modification: MEM EQU changed from 62 to 64 (64K system), and
four 8080-dialect "A,M" operands changed to the Z80 equivalent "A,(HL)".
Assembled with pasmo 0.5.3.

The original CPM.SYS binary (cpm22-b.zip, Xerox 1800 distribution) was
also obtained from the same site as a cross-check.

BIOS (bios.asm / bios.bin)
--------------------------

Written for the bw-board project.  MIT license.  No Digital Research code.
Console: MC6850 ACIA at ports $80/$81.
Disk: host-side RAM-disk controller via ports $10–$15.


